slot. for Android: a Game Boy Color door's fade on the sides as in the middle.
From a door's fade (PK_WIDE_SCENE_FADE, or a whole white or black frame)
until the next map is read and fully mixed in, the glow past the game's
edges follows the frame at its own brightness and without lagging behind
it, and the frozen scene gives way to it in 4 frames instead of 16: the
sides stayed grey while Pokemon Crystal's middle went white, then showed
dark bands as the town (read while the screen was still white) mixed in.
While the frame is all white or black the sides are the glow alone; the
next map mixes in once the game fades it in: going in, the room is read on
the first white frame (never a FADE scene) and its dark outside, which
doesn't fade with the game's colours, darkened the window's edges. Game
Boy games keep their doors as they were (right in Pokemon Blue).

